// TAG-189 Example 12.14 Arbitrated Places
// Deterministic arbitration test: exactly one member of the
// arbitration group carries a value per row, and that member wins
// without competition (per the book: "if only one place has
// content, the content will flow through the arbiter without
// competition").
//
// The arbitration group is {{$place1 $place2}}. Its members become
// the testbench's input ports; `next` is the output.
//
// The both-members-valid case ("they compete; it cannot be
// predetermined which content will flow") is deferred until the
// vector format can express leftover-state or nondeterministic
// expectations.
//
// `null` means the wire carries no content this row.
// `-` on an output means "no assertion" (don't-care); used only if
//   needed. Every row below asserts its expected `next`.

@dut(Arbiter)
@vectors(place1, place2 : next)
@mode(wavefront)

// Only place1 has content. It wins; next carries K.
K, null : K

// Only place2 has content. It wins; next carries L.
null, L : L